The umoria postings were horribly botched.  If you can use ftp, then
you can get a good copy via anonymous ftp from my moria archive
on kukulcan.Berkeley.EDU.  Otherwise...

There are 6 parts (6, 9, 24, 26, 28, 30) that will fail and
give you this error message.  This is because there are 6 files (each in
a different part) that do not end in a newline, and shar archives containing
such a file will fail.  What you can do is search for a copy of the string
END_OF_FILE which does not start at the beginning of a line, and put
a newline in front of it so that it will be on a line by itself.  Then delete
the extracted copy of the file you just added a newline to because it will
be corrupted.  Then the shar archives will extract properly.  Those
six files will give 'wrong number of characters extracted' messages because
of that extra newline, ignore those messages.  

There is one Mac documentation file, ScrnMgr.doc, which is in a Mac format,
i.e. each paragraph is one line.  The longest line in this file is about 1000
characters.  This file is a total loss; it won't extract properly, and
you can't fix it.

There are also a four source files at the top level which should be in
the source directory, and six files which are missing.  Fortunately
none of the missing files are important.  I will try to create a patch
file which will fix all of these problems and send that to comp.sources.games.

As penance for my sins, I have made some modifications to r$'s cshar
package so that it won't create bad shar files like it did for
umoria.  Also, I have fixed a number of bugs and added a number
of useful (to me at least) new features.  If Rich accepts my changes,
they will help prevent such problems in the future.

